{
    "background_story": "Ermias was a gentle soul with a passion for botany. Growing up in the rolling hills of Tuscany, he spent most of his childhood exploring the countryside and learning about the local flora. Among his favorite flowers was the delicate cyclamen, with its heart-shaped leaves and vibrant petals. As a young adult, Ermias became a renowned horticulturist, specializing in the cultivation of rare and exotic plants. He spent years perfecting his craft, and his nursery became a haven for cyclamen enthusiasts from around the world. Ermias' love for the cyclamen went beyond its beauty; he believed that its unique shape and color symbolized the resilience and adaptability of the human spirit. He often gifted cyclamen plants to those in need of comfort, spreading joy and hope wherever he went.",
